  "question": {
    "text": "A planet revolves about the sun in an elliptical orbit of semi-major axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The areal velocity of the planet when it is nearest to the sun is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.4</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the least distance between the planet and the sun is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then the minimum speed of the planet is"
